WEBVTT

00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:35.150
Japonet! Japonet!

00:01:35.150 --> 00:01:38.940
Japonet's prices are as low as they come!

00:01:39.930 --> 00:01:42.160
Japonet TV Shopping!

00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:44.570
Hey there, viewers!

00:01:44.570 --> 00:01:48.260
Tired out from living it up all summer vacation?

00:01:48.260 --> 00:01:49.540
We have just the thing!

00:01:49.540 --> 00:01:51.180
Presenting:

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:54.050
the form-fitting giant pillow!

00:01:54.050 --> 00:01:55.400
Still with me?

00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:57.960
Now watch and pay attention.

00:01:59.130 --> 00:02:02.870
This is not a pillow you hug,
but rather one that hugs you.

00:02:02.870 --> 00:02:06.350
Such comfort can make you lose all motivation...

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:11.310
Let's see.

00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:13.400
Zero-one-two...

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:13.820
Ahem.

00:02:15.010 --> 00:02:17.200
And what business do you have with Japonet?

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:22.570
W-Well, you see, Dandy Takematsu and me go way back,

00:02:22.570 --> 00:02:25.870
and I was just wondering how he'd been lately...

00:02:27.590 --> 00:02:29.000
When'd you meet <i>him</i>?!

00:02:30.550 --> 00:02:32.730
You're after that pillow, aren't you?

00:02:32.730 --> 00:02:35.130
Don't be so wasteful. You have that cat one.

00:02:41.020 --> 00:02:42.180
Umaru!

00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:43.660
Wake up, Umaru!

00:02:43.660 --> 00:02:45.550
You're gonna love what I've bought!

00:02:46.710 --> 00:02:48.990
What're you talking about, Onii-chan?

00:02:48.990 --> 00:02:51.660
I just now came back from shopping!

00:02:51.660 --> 00:02:52.940
Presenting...

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:54.610
That pillow!

00:02:55.120 --> 00:02:55.800
Precisely!

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:57.870
The de-motivating pillow!

00:02:57.870 --> 00:02:58.560
Huh?

00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:00.670
Was that was it was called?

00:03:00.670 --> 00:03:02.670
Rest assured, that's correct!

00:03:02.670 --> 00:03:05.500
Onii-chan, you sound like you're reading from a script.

00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:07.240
Now, pay attention!

00:03:07.240 --> 00:03:08.270
Hup!

00:03:09.740 --> 00:03:11.250
It molds to your body!

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:15.480
I'm losing all motivation...

00:03:19.080 --> 00:03:24.180
My no-nonsense brother has turned into a couch potato in an instant!

00:03:26.790 --> 00:03:31.790
Every cell in my body is screaming, "This pillow is dangerous!"

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:35.710
<i>Still, just a short nap couldn't...</i>

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:40.530
Japonekko! Japonekko!

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:44.310
Japonet's prices will knock your socks off!

00:03:47.430 --> 00:03:47.990
Hey there!

00:03:47.990 --> 00:03:50.830
Today, we bring you this product!

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:53.360
The form-fitting pillow!

00:03:53.360 --> 00:03:56.870
It's the most cutting-edge pillow ever devised by human technology!

00:03:57.630 --> 00:04:02.960
Incredibly, it automatically shapes itself for optimal relaxation!

00:04:04.550 --> 00:04:06.850
Here's the secret:

00:04:06.850 --> 00:04:11.140
An embedded AI chip automatically
adjusts it between five configurations!

00:04:12.350 --> 00:04:13.590
And that's not all!

00:04:13.590 --> 00:04:17.830
Our unique technology allows you to even ride around on its back!

00:04:17.830 --> 00:04:21.160
Forward! Turning!
Any way you please!

00:04:22.570 --> 00:04:23.910
But wait, there's more!

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:28.520
It can serve drinks and even
grind XP for you while you sleep!

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:32.540
Call now, and we'll include a special bonus!

00:04:46.430 --> 00:04:49.510
This exclusive offer includes
a booster that will let you fly!

00:04:49.850 --> 00:04:51.800
So call now!

00:04:51.800 --> 00:04:53.680
Toll-free, 012—

00:04:59.830 --> 00:05:01.240
What is it?

00:05:01.240 --> 00:05:04.980
Oh, um, just a dream.

00:05:04.980 --> 00:05:06.270
All right.

00:05:21.370 --> 00:05:26.380
<i>Wasn't this the Necolumbus I won with Onii-chan at the rock-paper-scissors tournament?</i>

00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:29.430
<i>I've barely touched it lately.</i>

00:05:29.850 --> 00:05:31.900
It was probably feeling lonely.

00:05:33.180 --> 00:05:34.930
Wait, that's not right!

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:38.230
I bought this one off an online auction!

00:05:43.670 --> 00:05:45.440
Come on, Umaru, wake up.

00:05:45.930 --> 00:05:47.760
It's time to go to school.

00:05:56.620 --> 00:06:00.380
Now, I'd like to play my latest song for you folks.

00:06:00.380 --> 00:06:04.200
"Oh! Sexy Summer 201..."

00:06:06.150 --> 00:06:08.440
This pillow is <i>definitely</i> bad news.

00:06:08.440 --> 00:06:09.180
Yeah.

00:06:11.930 --> 00:06:13.930
S-Sylphine-san.

00:06:13.930 --> 00:06:15.600
Why hello, Ebitake-san.

00:06:15.600 --> 00:06:18.000
I quite enjoyed our outing to the beach.

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:19.560
M-Me too.

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:20.860
Also, it's Ebina.

00:06:20.860 --> 00:06:23.500
Was there something you wished to ask me?

00:06:23.500 --> 00:06:28.000
Oh, I was just curious why you looked so cheerful.

00:06:29.210 --> 00:06:33.660
I'm off to meet my former rival and current bosom buddy after this.

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:35.660
Bosom...

00:06:35.660 --> 00:06:38.580
Oh, you made plans to meet a friend?

00:06:38.580 --> 00:06:40.650
I made nothing of the sort!

00:06:40.650 --> 00:06:41.250
Huh?

00:06:41.250 --> 00:06:45.300
No plans are needed when fate shall guide us to each other!

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:48.480
And with that, Ebishima-san, I bid you adieu!

00:06:48.480 --> 00:06:50.180
It's Ebina!

00:06:51.530 --> 00:06:54.430
I was hoping we could become better friends...

00:06:54.430 --> 00:06:55.690
As I was saying...

00:06:56.840 --> 00:06:58.790
Is something the matter, Umaru-san?

00:06:58.790 --> 00:07:00.200
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:07:00.200 --> 00:07:02.810
I just remembered some urgent business.

00:07:06.810 --> 00:07:09.780
I knew I'd find you at the arcade, UMR-san!

00:07:09.780 --> 00:07:13.180
Now, let's have a meeting to discuss how to defeat Umaru-san!

00:07:13.180 --> 00:07:15.220
Um, TSF-san,

00:07:15.220 --> 00:07:18.520
I'd prefer if we made plans in advance next time.

00:07:18.520 --> 00:07:20.950
Oh, in advance?

00:07:20.950 --> 00:07:21.920
Yeah...

00:07:22.350 --> 00:07:25.130
<i>I had to dash to get into my disguise.</i>

00:07:25.850 --> 00:07:27.210
Oh, a convenience store.

00:07:28.240 --> 00:07:31.080
I'm kinda thirsty, so I'd like to buy a cola.

00:07:31.080 --> 00:07:33.010
Then I shall accompany you!

00:07:37.130 --> 00:07:38.810
I-I don't believe it!

00:07:39.140 --> 00:07:40.020
What is it?

00:07:40.450 --> 00:07:45.030
It's the Patsune Migu convenience store prize lottery that's been sold out everywhere!

00:07:45.030 --> 00:07:47.780
I can't believe they still have it in stock!

00:07:47.780 --> 00:07:52.000
And the A-rank prize, the ultra-rare
Patsune Migu Nendro figure, hasn't been won yet!

00:07:55.240 --> 00:07:56.950
<i>I'm critically low on ammo!</i>

00:08:01.600 --> 00:08:05.010
TSF-san, do you mind if I take
a moment to play this lottery?

00:08:05.010 --> 00:08:06.880
Hm? Go ahead.

00:08:13.280 --> 00:08:16.100
<i>There is one rule when you draw from a convenience store lottery.</i>

00:08:16.680 --> 00:08:18.280
<i>Namely, do it quickly!</i>

00:08:19.280 --> 00:08:21.960
<i>This is a convenience store, after all.</i>

00:08:21.960 --> 00:08:26.500
<i>It would be inconsiderate to rummage around for ages while other customers are waiting.</i>

00:08:26.500 --> 00:08:29.690
<i>Plus, it's kind of embarrassing.</i>

00:08:31.220 --> 00:08:34.160
<i>The probability of drawing the A-rank prize is one in fifty.</i>

00:08:34.160 --> 00:08:39.050
<i>Since several people have already drawn, it's likely down to one in thirty.</i>

00:08:39.050 --> 00:08:43.000
<i>With two draws, that's a one in fifteen chance.</i>

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:46.000
<i>One in fifteen. Not bad at all.</i>

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:46.920
<i>I can do it.</i>

00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:48.880
<i>I have the good luck to pull it off!</i>

00:09:02.610 --> 00:09:04.850
<i>How did I get the second-lowest prize both times?!</i>

00:09:04.850 --> 00:09:07.350
<i>I don't have any use for these dumb notebooks!</i>

00:09:07.740 --> 00:09:09.090
UMR-san.

00:09:09.880 --> 00:09:11.930
You are my friend.

00:09:11.930 --> 00:09:15.620
Allow me to splendidly avenge your defeat!

00:09:17.450 --> 00:09:20.200
T-TSF-san...

00:09:23.910 --> 00:09:26.080
How splendidly charming!

00:09:26.480 --> 00:09:28.170
<i>She got the lowest prize every time.</i>

00:09:29.540 --> 00:09:32.050
<i>We couldn't even win anything good between the two of us.</i>

00:09:32.050 --> 00:09:34.520
<i>The greatest danger of a prize lottery is thinking,</i>

00:09:34.520 --> 00:09:36.550
"But I'll win it on the next draw!"

00:09:36.550 --> 00:09:40.050
<i>That vain hope has snared many a gambler.</i>

00:09:42.580 --> 00:09:45.220
UMR-san, are you sure you don't want these?

00:09:45.220 --> 00:09:46.850
Yeah, they're yours.

00:09:46.850 --> 00:09:48.510
How lovely!

00:09:49.230 --> 00:09:53.380
<i>If I hurry home and get some more cash...</i>

00:09:53.380 --> 00:09:56.530
<i>Or even better, borrow Onii-chan's
card for just a bit...</i>

00:09:56.530 --> 00:09:57.860
UMR-san!

00:09:58.490 --> 00:10:02.330
Look! We can use these to plan when we next meet!

00:10:06.580 --> 00:10:09.210
What's up? You're in quite the good mood.

00:10:10.920 --> 00:10:11.930
You think so?

00:10:27.060 --> 00:10:28.810
I-I...

00:10:28.810 --> 00:10:31.190
It's Korean barbecue time!

00:10:31.190 --> 00:10:35.520
O-Onii-chan, we're eating out at a Korean barbecue place!

00:10:35.520 --> 00:10:37.820
Can we really afford to splurge like this?

00:10:37.820 --> 00:10:39.960
O-Of course!

00:10:39.960 --> 00:10:42.200
I just got my paycheck.

00:10:48.650 --> 00:10:50.210
I can't wait any longer!

00:10:50.210 --> 00:10:51.210
Go ahead!

00:10:51.210 --> 00:10:52.590
No need to hold back!

00:10:52.590 --> 00:10:53.480
But...

00:10:53.930 --> 00:10:56.640
we really should have invited Ebina-chan.

00:10:56.640 --> 00:10:58.000
She'd have liked this.

00:10:58.000 --> 00:10:59.750
It's unfortunate, but she wasn't home.

00:10:59.750 --> 00:11:01.210
We'll invite her next time.

00:11:01.210 --> 00:11:01.970
Okay.

00:11:02.430 --> 00:11:04.000
Then let's get started...

00:11:04.000 --> 00:11:04.930
Hang on, Umaru.

00:11:06.620 --> 00:11:08.370
Wh-Why?

00:11:08.850 --> 00:11:12.610
Will you allow me to take charge of grilling the meat?

00:11:13.080 --> 00:11:15.860
Th-Those eyes mean business!

00:11:16.250 --> 00:11:19.950
Am I witnessing a legendary Barbecue Shogun?!

00:11:28.700 --> 00:11:30.330
First is the salted beef tongue with scallions!

00:11:35.340 --> 00:11:38.960
<i>Korean barbecue is lovely in a group,</i>

00:11:39.640 --> 00:11:43.720
<i>but the occasional solo experience has its own charms.</i>

00:11:44.400 --> 00:11:46.220
<i>One piece at a time, just enough for yourself.</i>

00:11:46.990 --> 00:11:50.520
<i>In a group, it's easy to add too much meat in your excitement,</i>

00:11:50.520 --> 00:11:53.480
<i>causing the temperature of the grill to drop.</i>

00:11:55.940 --> 00:11:58.330
Don't you think that's too much at once?

00:11:58.330 --> 00:11:59.830
O-Oh, no!

00:11:59.830 --> 00:12:01.490
What have I done?!

00:12:01.490 --> 00:12:04.620
O-Onii-chan got careless with excitement.

00:12:05.120 --> 00:12:07.960
<i>If you turn the meat over, the scallions will fall off,</i>

00:12:07.960 --> 00:12:09.950
<i>so instead, fold it in two like so.</i>

00:12:10.980 --> 00:12:13.830
<i>Rest assured, the meat will still cook through.</i>

00:12:19.430 --> 00:12:21.310
So good, eh?

00:12:25.970 --> 00:12:28.120
All the scallions fell off!

00:12:28.120 --> 00:12:29.560
S-Sorry!

00:12:29.560 --> 00:12:31.360
I'll be more careful next—

00:12:32.730 --> 00:12:35.530
The scallions caught fire!

00:12:37.720 --> 00:12:41.110
<i>The salted tongue serves as a light palate refresher</i>

00:12:41.110 --> 00:12:44.240
<i>before the crown jewel of Korean barbecue, the galbi.</i>

00:12:44.910 --> 00:12:47.950
<i>The white marbling that
criss-crosses the crimson canvas</i>

00:12:47.950 --> 00:12:52.750
<i>creates a contrast that can only be called art.</i>

00:12:53.330 --> 00:12:56.800
<i>As the meat grills, the dripping fat dances in the charcoal flames,</i>

00:12:56.800 --> 00:13:01.890
<i>sizzling in a harmony as sweet as a Siren's song.</i>

00:13:07.720 --> 00:13:10.260
Oh geez, dis is good too.

00:13:14.070 --> 00:13:16.940
Now the fat from the galbi's caught fire!

00:13:16.940 --> 00:13:19.770
I overcooked it again!

00:13:23.130 --> 00:13:26.060
<i>You could say rice is the heart of a Korean barbecue meal.</i>

00:13:26.060 --> 00:13:28.600
<i>The tender, loving Koshihikari rice of Akita</i>

00:13:28.600 --> 00:13:31.240
<i>accepts any kind of meat into its embrace.</i>

00:13:31.990 --> 00:13:34.480
<i>By absorbing the marinade and juices from the meat,</i>

00:13:34.480 --> 00:13:39.130
<i>the sweet rice elevates its taste to new heights.</i>

00:13:42.630 --> 00:13:46.510
It makes a fella real proud to be from Akita.

00:13:48.500 --> 00:13:50.450
Forgive me, Umaru.

00:13:50.450 --> 00:13:53.190
This fine meat was wasted on my incompetence.

00:13:56.920 --> 00:13:57.980
Here.

00:13:57.980 --> 00:14:00.180
Th-This is...

00:14:00.180 --> 00:14:02.320
A piece of galbi that I was tending to.

00:14:02.800 --> 00:14:04.190
That one's for you.

00:14:04.930 --> 00:14:05.960
Umaru...

00:14:11.060 --> 00:14:12.650
Now, let's eat!

00:14:12.650 --> 00:14:13.510
Yeah. let's.

00:14:13.510 --> 00:14:14.580
Okay!

00:14:22.040 --> 00:14:24.800
Delish!

00:14:27.260 --> 00:14:29.580
<i>Not only were the meat and rice delicious,</i>

00:14:29.580 --> 00:14:32.200
<i>the vegetables were organic and
delivered straight from the farm,</i>

00:14:32.200 --> 00:14:34.920
<i>and the seafood was freshly caught this morning.</i>

00:14:34.920 --> 00:14:36.660
<i>I'm in bliss.</i>

00:14:37.650 --> 00:14:38.060
<i>Now, then.</i>

00:14:38.060 --> 00:14:39.440
Let's see...

00:14:40.070 --> 00:14:42.560
<i>I think I'm ready for another round.</i>

00:14:43.830 --> 00:14:45.440
What a meal.

00:14:45.440 --> 00:14:49.890
It doesn't get better than washing down juicy meat with cola, Onii-chan.

00:14:49.890 --> 00:14:50.950
Good to hear.

00:14:50.950 --> 00:14:51.160
We're ready to pay.

00:14:51.160 --> 00:14:52.830
I'm ready to pay.

00:14:54.110 --> 00:14:56.040
Huh? Ebina-chan?

00:14:56.040 --> 00:14:58.990
U-Umaru-chan and Onii-san,

00:14:58.990 --> 00:15:00.530
you came for barbecue too?

00:15:02.540 --> 00:15:03.960
<i>Solo Korean barbecue?</i>

00:15:03.960 --> 00:15:05.470
<i>That's pretty advanced.</i>

00:15:10.790 --> 00:15:12.750
<i>Another tiring day.</i>

00:15:12.750 --> 00:15:14.940
<i>I'll just make something simple for dinner.</i>

00:15:17.230 --> 00:15:18.230
I'm home.

00:15:19.870 --> 00:15:21.690
Monster!

00:15:21.690 --> 00:15:23.110
Wh-What's this, now?

00:15:23.110 --> 00:15:25.650
Trick or treat!

00:15:26.060 --> 00:15:27.050
Right.

00:15:27.050 --> 00:15:29.490
It's Halloween season, isn't it?

00:15:29.490 --> 00:15:30.940
That's perfect.

00:15:30.940 --> 00:15:32.990
I happened to buy some snacks today.

00:15:35.430 --> 00:15:35.990
Here.

00:15:35.990 --> 00:15:37.770
Happy Halloween!

00:15:40.000 --> 00:15:43.560
Come on, don't you have any Western snacks?

00:15:43.560 --> 00:15:46.160
Onii-chan, go and buy some!

00:15:46.160 --> 00:15:47.460
No way.

00:15:47.460 --> 00:15:49.380
I just got home.

00:15:49.800 --> 00:15:51.510
And those are perfectly good rice crackers.

00:15:51.510 --> 00:15:53.930
It's the spirit that counts!

00:15:54.920 --> 00:15:58.180
G-Give us treats, o-or we'll play a trick...

00:15:59.930 --> 00:16:03.350
Well done, Kirie-chan! You got him good!

00:16:03.350 --> 00:16:04.800
Thank you, Master!

00:16:04.800 --> 00:16:07.920
Halloween's not just an excuse to play pranks, you know!

00:16:10.070 --> 00:16:13.120
So why the sudden Halloween spirit?

00:16:13.120 --> 00:16:16.630
It came up while me and Kirie-chan were hanging out today.

00:16:18.130 --> 00:16:20.330
It's October already, isn't it?

00:16:20.330 --> 00:16:21.460
Yeah.

00:16:21.460 --> 00:16:23.290
So you've eaten plenty of snacks already!

00:16:23.960 --> 00:16:25.110
On that subject,

00:16:25.110 --> 00:16:27.340
what comes to mind when you think of October?

00:16:28.210 --> 00:16:29.000
Halloween!

00:16:29.000 --> 00:16:29.640
Ghosts!

00:16:29.640 --> 00:16:30.550
Treats!

00:16:33.780 --> 00:16:35.310
Um...

00:16:35.720 --> 00:16:39.140
So what exactly do you do on Halloween, anyway?

00:16:39.570 --> 00:16:42.850
Dress up in costume, I guess?

00:16:43.180 --> 00:16:44.280
Costume?

00:16:46.040 --> 00:16:48.230
I'm pretty sure I have something...

00:16:49.480 --> 00:16:52.110
Which brings us to the present, Onii-chan!

00:16:53.410 --> 00:16:55.240
Monster!

00:16:59.420 --> 00:17:00.520
All right.

00:17:00.520 --> 00:17:02.930
I'll pick up a few more things
and come right back.

00:17:04.940 --> 00:17:08.400
Say, Onii-chan's the only one not in costume.

00:17:08.400 --> 00:17:09.520
You're right.

00:17:09.520 --> 00:17:11.300
Let's prepare him one!

00:17:30.110 --> 00:17:31.320
Pumpkin gratin!

00:17:31.800 --> 00:17:33.990
Pumpkin pizza and pumpkin sauté!

00:17:33.990 --> 00:17:36.700
Pumpkin omelette rice and pumpkin soup!

00:17:37.830 --> 00:17:39.460
It looks great!

00:17:39.460 --> 00:17:43.270
Halloween is a day to give thanks for the autumn harvest.

00:17:43.270 --> 00:17:45.440
It's only proper to celebrate it with pumpkin dishes.

00:17:45.440 --> 00:17:48.380
Now you both talk <i>and</i> look like a chef, Onii-chan!

00:17:48.790 --> 00:17:50.780
What's this outfit supposed to be, anyway?

00:17:50.780 --> 00:17:52.320
It's covered in blood.

00:17:52.320 --> 00:17:56.010
It's the zombie chef from the game <i>Delicious Zombie</i>.

00:18:02.640 --> 00:18:04.600
Could you dress me up as something less gruesome?

00:18:04.600 --> 00:18:05.770
<i>But it suits you.</i>

00:18:05.770 --> 00:18:07.180
Sheesh.

00:18:08.440 --> 00:18:10.010
Oh, sounds like it's done.

00:18:11.210 --> 00:18:13.030
I baked a pumpkin pie!

00:18:18.480 --> 00:18:20.780
So sweet!

00:18:21.190 --> 00:18:23.300
It feels like we're in a different country!

00:18:23.300 --> 00:18:26.620
Kirie-chan, we might as well be!

00:18:40.930 --> 00:18:43.430
Happy Halloween!

00:18:43.810 --> 00:18:44.930
Monster!

00:18:48.860 --> 00:18:51.150
The soft touch of this futon...

00:18:51.150 --> 00:18:54.250
If only I could live my whole life atop it.

00:18:55.420 --> 00:18:58.910
But I've got class tomorrow, class the day after...

00:18:58.910 --> 00:19:00.860
It's all so much effort.

00:19:03.400 --> 00:19:07.390
Can't I go back to the daily
paradise of summer vacation?

00:19:07.970 --> 00:19:09.460
Oh, summer vacation.

00:19:09.460 --> 00:19:13.040
After all this time, I still can't forget you.

00:19:13.470 --> 00:19:15.280
Well, it's fall now,

00:19:15.280 --> 00:19:18.420
so maybe a typhoon will blow in and school will get canceled.

00:19:19.440 --> 00:19:20.680
Get up, Umaru!

00:19:20.680 --> 00:19:22.800
It's time for school!

00:19:22.800 --> 00:19:24.930
Hurry and eat your breakfast, then get ready to go!

00:19:26.220 --> 00:19:28.180
<i>I wanna stay home!</i>

00:19:28.890 --> 00:19:31.590
I... think I have a fever.

00:19:31.590 --> 00:19:32.250
Huh?

00:19:35.720 --> 00:19:37.260
It's mild, but you do.

00:19:38.820 --> 00:19:41.600
You'd better stay home, just to be sure.

00:19:42.680 --> 00:19:46.880
Get plenty of rest. I'll try to come home early.

00:19:46.880 --> 00:19:48.330
O-Okay.

00:19:49.040 --> 00:19:51.650
I'm sorry you waited here for nothing, Ebina-chan.

00:19:51.650 --> 00:19:53.080
I-It's fine.

00:19:53.080 --> 00:19:55.350
I hope Umaru-chan's okay.

00:19:55.350 --> 00:19:56.920
Uh-oh, we're going to be late!

00:19:56.920 --> 00:19:58.250
R-Right!

00:20:03.220 --> 00:20:07.470
<i>I-I've never skipped school before.</i>

00:20:08.000 --> 00:20:09.980
<i>Secret Technique: Friction Fever!</i>

00:20:11.150 --> 00:20:12.570
<i>What now?</i>

00:20:13.310 --> 00:20:15.000
<i>Well...</i>

00:20:15.000 --> 00:20:15.920
<i>What the heck!</i>

00:20:17.070 --> 00:20:19.210
There's no turning back now that I've skipped!

00:20:19.210 --> 00:20:21.490
Slacking off must have been in the cards today!

00:20:21.490 --> 00:20:24.990
So without further ado, time to laze to my heart's content!

00:20:43.460 --> 00:20:46.010
<i>It feels like time is passing so slowly.</i>

00:20:46.600 --> 00:20:49.640
<i>Was skipping school really such a good idea?</i>

00:20:51.810 --> 00:20:54.320
<i>So you lied to me, Umaru.</i>

00:20:54.320 --> 00:20:56.260
<i>That's low.</i>

00:20:56.260 --> 00:20:58.770
<i>I'm ashamed to have called you Master.</i>

00:20:58.770 --> 00:21:00.110
<i>Splendidly so!</i>

00:21:03.650 --> 00:21:06.630
I hope Umaru-chan's not too sick.

00:21:13.480 --> 00:21:15.590
Third period's starting already!

00:21:19.840 --> 00:21:21.550
Huh? Umaru-chan?

00:21:21.550 --> 00:21:23.340
I thought you were off sick today.

00:21:23.340 --> 00:21:25.500
Right... Well...

00:21:25.500 --> 00:21:28.470
I felt better, so I decided to come in.

00:21:28.470 --> 00:21:31.730
A-Are you okay, Umaru-chan?

00:21:31.730 --> 00:21:32.560
Yeah.

00:21:34.340 --> 00:21:35.940
You should take it easy—

00:21:35.940 --> 00:21:37.810
How splendid of you to come, Umaru-san!

00:21:38.810 --> 00:21:41.390
Just in time to face off in today's quiz!

00:21:41.390 --> 00:21:44.740
She's still recovering! Don't put pressure on her!

00:21:44.740 --> 00:21:45.290
Very well!

00:21:45.290 --> 00:21:48.030
As a handicap, I shall write only with my left hand!

00:21:48.030 --> 00:21:49.750
You're making absolutely no sense!

00:21:49.750 --> 00:21:51.580
Don't fight, please!

00:21:51.580 --> 00:21:53.760
I shall be splendidly victorious!

00:21:53.760 --> 00:21:54.580
I <i>said</i>, don't...

00:21:56.250 --> 00:21:57.960
Ah, your fever's gone down.

00:21:57.960 --> 00:22:00.650
Still, you should keep resting.

00:22:00.650 --> 00:22:01.840
Right...

00:22:02.840 --> 00:22:04.090
Onii-chan.

00:22:04.090 --> 00:22:04.860
Hm?

00:22:07.630 --> 00:22:08.340
Here.

00:22:11.040 --> 00:22:12.070
Umaru!

00:22:12.070 --> 00:22:14.400
I'm sorry!
